//! Token exporters: one [`Exporter`] interface, one implementation per [`Target`].
//!
//! `crunk.toml` compiles to a [`TokenSet`]; each exporter turns that set into the text of one
//! generated file (`tokens.css`, the flat JSON export, the Tailwind theme mapping). Later targets
//! (DTCG, USS, a C# token class; docs/design/crunk.md section 2) are further implementations of
//! the same trait and one more [`Target`] variant, with no change to the write and drift code.
//!
//! The drift side is split so `TOKENS001` can compute its input without touching this crate's
//! I/O: [`render_managed`] is pure (the expected text of every configured file),
//! [`compare`] is pure (expected text against whatever text is on disk, or `None` when the file
//! is missing), and [`check`] / [`write_all`] are the disk-backed wrappers.
//!
//! ```
//! use std::path::Path;
//! use crunk_tokens::export::{Target, render_target};
//!
//! let spec = crunk_spec::parse_spec(
//!     crunk_spec::presets::DEFAULT,
//!     Path::new("crunk.toml"),
//!     Path::new("/proj"),
//! )
//! .unwrap();
//! let css = render_target(&spec, Target::Css).unwrap();
//! assert!(css.starts_with("/* GENERATED by crunk tokens"));
//! ```

